# Unlinked (`GenServer.start`) named singletons. The guard matched only
# `start_link` until now, so these were invisible to it rather than approved:
# an unlinked singleton is the MORE dangerous shape, since nothing supervises
# it, a crash takes its whole state with it and skips `terminate/2`, and
# nothing stops it on application shutdown.
#
# `shell/jobs.ex` starts under `Raxol.Agent.DynSup` whenever the agent subtree
# is running; the bare `start` is the fallback for a VM that has no subtree to
# supervise under (a plain script, a focused test). The other three are
# pre-existing and still take the bare path unconditionally.
packages/raxol_agent/lib/raxol/agent/shell/jobs.ex
packages/raxol_agent/lib/raxol/agent/probe/runner/pool.ex
packages/raxol_agent/lib/raxol/agent/spend_gate/reservations.ex
packages/raxol_symphony/lib/raxol/symphony/prompt_builder/memo.ex

# `Raxol.MCP.Client.Tables` owns the era-verdict table and the client-side
# origin breaker table, and it is named on purpose. ADR-0037 decision 2 needs
# the dual-era verdict to be per ORIGIN: an :ets table belongs to the process
# that created it, so a table created by a client would make the verdict per
# client and cache nothing useful, and one created by a transient process
# raises ArgumentError in whoever still holds the reference. Accepting
# [name: nil] would hand each caller its own cache, which is the defect.
packages/raxol_mcp/lib/raxol/mcp/client/tables.ex

# `Raxol.Web3.Supervisor` and `Raxol.Web3.Tables` are the same shape as the
# MCP pair above and were invisible for a plainer reason: the guard's roots
# did not include `packages/raxol_web3/lib` at all, so the package was never
# scanned. `Tables` owns the token-bucket, breaker, origin and cache tables
# for the whole node (ADR-0038 decision 5): a table belongs to the process
# that created it, so a per-caller owner spends a free-tier rate budget once
# per process, never trips a breaker on anyone else's failures, and leaves
# `ArgumentError` behind when it dies. That is the defect [name: nil] would
# reintroduce. `Supervisor` is its canonical supervisor.
packages/raxol_web3/lib/raxol/web3/supervisor.ex
packages/raxol_web3/lib/raxol/web3/tables.ex
